1
00:04:49,090 --> 00:04:55,090
Cute. Clever. Mischievous. Intelligent. Dangerous.

2
00:09:38,181 --> 00:09:44,181
Gremlins is a fantasy, horror, comedy film directed by Joe Dante.

3
00:14:27,272 --> 00:14:33,272
After receiving an exotic small animal as a Christmas gift, a young man inadvertently breaks three important rules
concerning his new pet, which unleashes a horde of malevolently mischievous creatures on a small town.

4
00:19:16,363 --> 00:19:22,363
Billy Peltzer, played by Zach Galligan.

5
00:24:05,454 --> 00:24:11,454
Kate Beringer, played by Phoebe Cates.

6
00:28:54,545 --> 00:29:00,545
Randall Peltzer, played by Hoyt Axton.

7
00:33:43,636 --> 00:33:49,636
Lynn Peltzer, played by Frances Lee McCain.

8
00:38:32,727 --> 00:38:38,727
Pete Fountaine, played by Corey Feldman.

9
00:43:21,818 --> 00:43:27,818
Grandfather (Mr. Wing), played by Keye Luke.

10
00:48:10,909 --> 00:48:16,909
Gremlins is a 1984 American black comedy horror film directed by Joe Dante, written by Chris Columbus and starring Zach Galligan,
Phoebe Cates, Hoyt Axton, Polly Holliday and Frances Lee McCain, with Howie Mandel providing the voice of Gizmo the Mogwai.

11
00:52:59,999 --> 00:53:05,999
It draws on legends of folkloric mischievous creatures that cause
malfunctions—"gremlins"—in the British Royal Air Force going back to World War II.

12
00:57:49,090 --> 00:57:55,090
The story follows Billy Peltzer, who receives Gizmo as a pet, who then spawns more of his kind that evolve
into the titular imp-like monsters that wreak havoc on Billy's hometown during Christmas Eve.

13
01:02:38,181 --> 01:02:44,181
The film was accompanied by a large merchandising campaign and
juxtaposes black comedy with a Christmas time setting.

14
01:07:27,272 --> 01:07:33,272
Steven Spielberg was the executive producer, with the
film being produced by Michael Finnell.

15
01:12:16,363 --> 01:12:22,363
Gremlins was theatrically released on June 8, 1984, by Warner Bros.

16
01:17:05,454 --> 01:17:11,454
to critical and commercial success.

17
01:21:54,545 --> 01:22:00,545
However, it was heavily criticized for some of its more violent sequences.

18
01:26:43,636 --> 01:26:49,636
In response to this and to similar complaints about Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom, Spielberg suggested that the Motion Picture
Association of America (MPAA) alter its rating system, which it did within two months of the film's release, creating a new PG-13 rating.

19
01:31:32,727 --> 01:31:38,727
It was followed by a sequel, Gremlins 2: The New Batch (1990), while a
third film is set to be released on November 19, 2027.

20
01:36:21,818 --> 01:36:27,818
The film explores themes of small town, monster, holiday, department store, pet.

21
01:41:10,909 --> 01:41:16,909
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
